  "note": "Tier 0 overlay for the offline stub, keyed by knowledge time. The two populated positions carry MEASURED Event Zero values taken from tests/fixtures/hindcast/event_zero_ab.json (snohomish-snoqualmie 2025-12-06 and skagit 2025-12-11) so the client is exercised against numbers the platform really produced, not invented ones. The early position is the strict knowledge-time state: no reference existed yet, so every Tier 0 statement is absent with its reason. The susceptibility band is derived from the same fixture percentile using the shipped BAND_EDGES (25/75/90) so the panel shows the real contrast the design exists for: a MODERATE band beside a large, high-ranked change. Each position is a HALF-OPEN window [from, until). A knowledge time outside every window gets no overlay at all, and LIVE mode (no as_of) is deliberately one of those: this stub has no live Tier 0 data, and serving December 2025 values as though they were current would be the exact staleness the replay tests exist to forbid.",
